            <ArticleTitle>Persistent anterior hip pain in young adults: current aspects of diagnosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>61-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Persistent anterior hip pain, in young adults, presents a diagnostic and treatment challenge to hip surgeons. Diagnosis, in some cases, is difficult because available diagnostic tools are not very reliable, resulting in a difficult decision making process. This article discusses the possible causes, current knowledge of the condition and outlines a method to approach this difficult problem.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
